{
  "configuration_id": "config_008",
  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_011: multimodal, singleprofile, scvi_n200+resnet50, concat, acc≈0.536), the most critical uncertainty is whether the multimodal fusion is actually adding value over a unimodal baseline. config_008 (rna_only, singleprofile, scvi_n200) is the cleanest ablation: it keeps the exact same RNA encoder and profile setting as config_011 while removing only the image branch. This isolates the contribution of the image modality and the fusion step. If RNA alone performs comparably (~0.53+), the added complexity of multimodal fusion is questionable and subsequent experiments should focus on improving the RNA representation or trying a different image encoder. If RNA alone is substantially worse, it confirms the image modality is essential and justifies investing further in fusion/aggregation design. This single-variable comparison is the highest-information experiment under a limited budget, as it answers the foundational 'does multimodal help?' question before spending experiments on secondary design choices like fusion type, aggregation, or multiprofile settings."
}

